  "question": {
    "text": "A wire fixed at the upper end stretches by length by applying a force F. The work done in stretching is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{F} / 2$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{F} \\ell$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$2 \\mathrm{~F} \\ell$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{F} \\ell / 2$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Work done $=\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{kx}^2=\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{k} \\ell^2$ where $\\ell$ is the total extensions.\n$$\n=\\frac{1}{2}(\\mathrm{k} \\ell) \\ell=\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{~F} \\ell\n$$"
  }
}